{
  "about": [
    "The gentle reminder's thread, one shared scenario run through both layers (L121): src/domain's ladder.test.ts and @pinkoo/nag's RulesTest (its copy is packages/pinkoo-nag/test/thread-scenarios.json; the integrator checks the two with cmp). The rules are docs/product.md > Nagging, The pace, Her answers and A promise.",
    "Times are wall-clock local times in `zone`. Each case is one dose nobody takes; the phone is locked and every access is granted, so each step posts what it carries.",
    "`pace` names one of `paces` or is a pace object { firstMin, thenMin, repeatFirstMin, repeatEveryMin, repeats } (plan shape v2's NagLadder). firstMin: Notificacao to De novo. thenMin: to each next step on (Tela cheia, then the alarm 'Só se passar de tudo'). Repeats: the first repeatFirstMin after the last step, the others repeatEveryMin apart. A step that's off takes no time.",
    "`steps` is the plan's { bubble, fullScreen, unlock }; `alarm` is the dose's off | afterAll | onTime.",
    "`events` are her answers, applied in time order; an event at the same minute as a fire comes after it. do: notNow ('Agora não': the next step moves to max(when it was due, the tap + that step's own gap), never moving the step), promise (until: the deadline; nothing comes for the dose until then), swipe and open (change nothing).",
    "`expect` is every fire of the dose in order, and nothing else before `dose.miss`. step: notify | again | full | alarm | repeat | deadline. rung: the reminders that reached her before this one (fires), capped at 4; a deadline counts as a fire but is not one of the repeats. sounding: the post plays her sound. folded: the step rides in the alarm's own notification, silent, and only the ring sounds ('Já na hora', and a promise's deadline for such a dose).",
    "`notNow` are probes, not events: what 'Agora não' would say if tapped at `at` (after every fire and event at or before `at`). kind: remind | alarm | wait; next: the time it names, null for wait (nothing comes before the dose is missed: after the last repeat, or a next step that would fall at or past dose.miss)."
  ],
